{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Narration moved out of the description to fit the review admission limit, per the P4 oversize remedy (\"move the narration into ticket comments or a session log\"). No acceptance criterion was dropped and no citation was weakened; all 23 ACs and the full config edit set remain in the plan.\n\n**ADR 0122 measurement detail (background, not a constraint).** `vector` beats the `fts5` baseline at semantic recall@5 0.876 vs 0.823, McNemar p=0.0213, recovering 13 pairs and losing 3. At k=10 the edge is indistinguishable (p=0.3438), which is why this ticket's k stays at 5.\n\n**Why the digest step is the weakest link.** `vector` is NOT distinguishable from `vector-raw`, which skips the digest (p=0.0654, p=0.0625). It survives only because `vector-raw` also fails to beat `fts5` (p=0.6636) — a non-transitive chain ADR 0122 states plainly. The digest is therefore carried on ADR 0122's adopted-configuration authority, not on a measured win over skipping it.\n\n**Backend availability probe (investigation record, 2026-11-02).** On this tree, with `[agents]` installed: `pydantic_ai.embeddings`, `.bedrock`, `.openai` and `.test` import; `.cohere`, `.google` and `.voyageai` raise `ImportError` naming their own optional group. That is the evidence behind the plan's \"a missing optional backend is expected, not a defect\" constraint.\n\n**Digest retry rate.** 2 of 630 digest calls returned nothing decodable, and both succeeded on retry — the basis for retrying case (a) exactly once and not retrying case (b).\n\n**Why a partially vectored corpus degrades rather than corrupts.** The full-current-key-coverage rule is a read-path rule, so an interrupted build affects only ranking quality for subsequent queries; stored entries are never mixed across embedding spaces and nothing on disk is left inconsistent.\n\n**4e89's plan attestation is already `stale-code`** (12 dependency files drifted as 47c8, 80a5, b505 and f10f landed), so editing this ticket no longer costs 4e89 a valid certificate."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793613321110734001,"uuid":"de838edf-2bb2-4006-9c0e-5a11b1358efe"}